<!-- qwerty_pkb keyboard layout — ATHENA variant (BlackBerry KEY2)
PID: ET9PLIDEnglish  SID: ET9SKIDPhonePad
UNEVEN ROW BANDS — matches the firmware's real per-row sensor allocation (measured via the visualizer
+ pen-on-dividers). The capacitive sensor (1080x525) splits into uneven row bands, NOT even rows:
  row1 QWERTY  sensor 0..90    (90px)
  row2 ASDF    sensor 90..270  (180px)
  row3 ZXCV    sensor 270..450 (180px)
  (row4 space  sensor 450..525 (75px) — not part of the letter KDB)
Columns are even (108px x 10 = 1080 = sensor width). Sensor->authored is 1:1 (offset 0, no scale), so
authored Y == sensor Y and every touch falls in the correct row band by construction. authored 1080x450.

RADY note (2026-08-14): the blob's swipe-segmentation thresholds all scale off NKL RADY (default =
home-row height = 180 here, vs the ~108 even-grid pitch the blob's decoder is tuned for). No single
RADY fits these uneven bands: 180 under-segments short tail hooks in the 90px row (hello->help,
0/10), an authored radiusY="108" over-segments transits through the 180px rows (done->songs) —
corpus evidence in remediation log §8.6-8.7. The layouts therefore carry NO radiusY (blob-parity
default) and the fix is the owned per-row-threshold gesture decoder (§8.7); the radiusY= attribute
remains available for experiments (kdb_nkl.c RADY note). -->

<keyboard
  primaryId="9"
  secondaryId="6"
  defaultLayoutWidth="1080"
  defaultLayoutHeight="450"
  addAltChars="true">

  <area>
    <key keyType="regional" keyLabel="Q" keyWidth="108dp" keyHeight="90dp" keyTop="0dp" keyLeft="0dp" />
